@page "/guide"
@layout StudentLayout
@inject ILesson Lesson

<PageTitle>C@(Lesson.Number.ToString("D2")) · @Lesson.Title</PageTitle>

<section id="learning" class="student-section">
    <h2>What you will learn</h2>
    <div class="student-cards">
        @for (var index = 0; index < Lesson.Concepts.Count; index++)
        {
            <article class="student-card"><h3><span class="student-number">@(index + 1)</span>@Lesson.Concepts[index]</h3><p>@steps[index]. Trace the rule in the architecture walkthrough and compare the displayed evidence.</p></article>
        }
    </div>
    <p class="student-note">@Lesson.Scope</p>
</section>

@code {
    // The first steps reported by the passing scenario, one per concept card.
    private static readonly string[] steps = ["Inherit omitted model", "Clear system with null", "Replace the entire tools list"];
}

<section class="student-section">
    <h2>Scenarios to investigate</h2>
    <div class="student-table">
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Expected outcome</th><th>Evidence to check</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var scenario in Lesson.Cases)
                {
                    <tr><td>@scenario.Label</td><td>@System.Text.Json.JsonSerializer.Serialize(scenario.Expected).Trim('"')</td><td><code>@((scenario.Checks ?? []).ToJsonString())</code></td></tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="run-guide" class="student-section">
    <h2>How to run this application</h2>
    <article class="student-step">
        <h3><span class="student-number">1</span>Install the .NET 10 SDK and open the application folder</h3>
        <p>Use the .NET 10 SDK or later. From the lesson-c11-csharp-app folder, restore the locked NuGet packages (including Anthropic 13.3.0).</p>
        <pre><code class="language-powershell">dotnet --version
dotnet restore</code></pre>
    </article>
    <article class="student-step">
        <h3><span class="student-number">2</span>Create your local .env file</h3>
        <p>No API key is required for the local experiment. Optional live commentary requires your own API key, agent ID and environment ID. It explains the local result; it does not activate the integration discussed in the lesson. Copy the example and edit the new file in your editor. The real .env is ignored by Git.</p>
        <pre><code class="language-powershell">Copy-Item .env.example .env
notepad .env</code></pre>
    </article>
    <article class="student-step">
        <h3><span class="student-number">3</span>Prepare resources or choose the local path</h3>
        <p>For the optional live path, set your API key, then run <code>dotnet run --project src/LessonC11.Setup</code> if you do not already have resource IDs. The tool creates the environment before a text-only agent, saves each ID immediately, and reuses IDs already configured. It uses CLAUDE_MODEL or the source default; choose a model available to your account. An uncertain network failure may have created a resource: inspect your account before retrying.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="student-step">
        <h3><span class="student-number">4</span>Start the application</h3>
        <p>Run the command below and wait for the printed server URL. Open <code>http://127.0.0.1:3011</code>. The terminal stays open while the server is running. If PORT differs, use that value instead.</p>
        <pre><code class="language-powershell">dotnet run --project src/LessonC11.Web</code></pre>
    </article>
    <article class="student-step">
        <h3><span class="student-number">5</span>Run and inspect the evidence</h3>
        <p>Select the first scenario, inspect its editable fields, press Run experiment, and compare the outcome and evidence with the table above. Select another scenario to investigate the boundary condition.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="student-step">
        <h3><span class="student-number">6</span>Verify and stop</h3>
        <p>Run the scenario tests below in a second terminal. Stop the web server with Ctrl+C. Local journal records are not production workflow state. Closing a browser tab does not confirm remote cancellation.</p>
        <pre><code class="language-powershell">dotnet test</code></pre>
    </article>
</section>

<section class="student-section">
    <h2>Create and understand .env</h2>
    <p>Copy the example rather than renaming it. Put your own values in .env; leave .env.example safe for sharing. Restart the server after changing configuration. PORT controls the local URL. An empty optional model value uses the source default.</p>
    <pre><code class="language-dotenv">ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key
CLAUDE_MANAGED_AGENT_ID=your_agent_id
CLAUDE_MANAGED_ENVIRONMENT_ID=your_environment_id
PORT=3011</code></pre>
    <p>The image below is a sanitized copy of a local .env file. All values except PORT are removed.</p>
    <img class="student-env" src="env-redacted.png" alt="Sanitized local .env configuration; secret values and resource IDs redacted">
</section>
